course: dictionary
lesson: 7359
title: Words built from smaller words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A playwright is a person who writes plays for the theatre. The word is built from two smaller words, play and wright. Wright is an old word for a maker, as in wheelwright, someone who makes wheels. So a playwright is a maker of plays.
explain: «Write», «right», «rite» and «wright» all sound the same, but they mean different things. In «The playwright wrote a new play», the clues are play and wrote, so the person must be a writer of plays. Context helps you choose the right meaning of the sound.
explain: In English lessons, a playwright writes scripts with characters, dialogue and stage directions. Famous playwrights include Shakespeare, Oscar Wilde and Arthur Miller. Often a playwright adds notes to the script telling actors how to speak or move.
fact: A playwright is a person who writes plays for the theatre.
fact: Playwright is a noun: one playwright, two playwrights.
fact: A script has characters, dialogue (the words they say) and stage directions (what they do).
fact: Famous playwrights include Shakespeare, Oscar Wilde and Arthur Miller.
fact: Wright is an old word for a maker, so a playwright is a maker of plays.
exercise: «The playwright wrote a new play for the school.» Who wrote the play? | *A playwright | A stage director | A ticket seller | An actor
exercise: What does a playwright write? | *Plays for the theatre | Songs for the radio | Letters to the Queen | Cars and buses
exercise: Playwright is made from two smaller words. Which two? | wrote and light | write and right | *play and wright | play and right
test: In a script, what are the words the characters say called? | *Dialogue | Stage directions | Tickets | Scenery
test: Write, right, rite and wright sound the same. In playwright, which one means a maker? | rite | *wright | right | write
exam: «The playwright's notes told the actor to whisper.» What is a playwright? | A person who sells theatre tickets | *A person who writes plays for the theatre | A person who builds the stage | A person who acts on stage
